# Tegra display controller nodes (/dev/tegra_dc_0..N, /dev/tegra_dc_ctrl).
#
# The HWC2 composer drives the display controller directly through these:
# it opens the head for the per-frame FLIP4 commit and a second node
# (/dev/tegra_dc_ctrl) for the blank-event stream its vsync worker reads.
# Under the generic device label those ioctls are refused, and it only
# looks harmless because this build runs permissive -- the denials are in
# the log on every frame (ioctlcmd 441d is FLIP4, 4415 the vblank
# subscription). The label and the rules below are what lets the
# composer run with SELinux enforcing.
#
# The stock HWC1 blob, kept for the fallback path, drives the same nodes
# and needs the same access. hal_graphics_composer is the attribute both
# the server and client domains belong to, and the pattern AOSP itself
# uses for this HAL's gpu_device and fb0 rules.

type tegra_dc_device, dev_type;

allow hal_graphics_composer tegra_dc_device:chr_file {
    open read write ioctl getattr map
};
